SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · Call 6:00 PM · 7:00 PM–7:45 PM · Robinson 
 Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 6:00 PM: dancers must b
 e checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 5:45 PM. BA: Call Time
  is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minute
 s before Call Time.\nACT I Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair an
 d Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHANG
 E — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal ar
 e the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1x
 WFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP f
 or Artillery: Soldiers: Artillery\, Brigade\, Infantry — Costume (you 
 provide): Black Seamless Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard Male Soldiers: 
 Black T-shirt\, Black tights\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light
  Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Wh
 ite Gloves\; Prop (BA provides): Brown gun\nLight Stage Makeup Instructi
 on Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye sha
 dow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/B
 lack eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the c
 heeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in th
 e stage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may 
 wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidel
 ines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent
  damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in 
 the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how si
 gnificant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or
  hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on 
 the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, cle
 an\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make
 -up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging 
 make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of s
 pray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment
  not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or b
 everage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not r
 emove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n
 •  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs follow
 ing their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•
   Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrob
 e policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or any
 thing that may damage or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
